"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched by Alex, with Sarah Tan as the lead and an initial budget of $500,000 for Phase One. The project has progressed through several stages: an initial kick-off in June, a call for R&D ideas in July (focusing on AI for data visualization), team expansions in September (adding members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing), and the completion of the design phase. Recent updates highlight a breakthrough in predictive analytics, the establishment of a strategic partnership with TechInnovate, and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The project is now moving into the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, with UI enhancements planned for October. A detailed progress report is scheduled for the staff meeting on November 20th, and feedback on the prototype is being sought until the end of November."
